		{
			dependencies: ["0EAF2C5B5EB755C5"]
			description: [
				"&l&8[&6PROJECT-MANAGER&8]&r&r"
				""
				"Another &abenefit&r for you. Your planet is rich with natural &aresources.&r It seems the &cnatives&r aren't using them anyways."
				"The ore here generates much differently from what you might expect, the veins are &6huge&r, and contain many stacks of ore."
				""
				"Your in-built mapping system can help you here. When you right click an &aore&r in a new vein, or a &bsurface rock&r it will be added to your map. You can &atoggle&r this with the button on the right of your map."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The full extent of ore generation is explained in the Tips and Tricks tab, but here is what you need to know:"
				""
				"&6-&r Ore veins generate in a grid. Every vein is spaced by &o(approximately)&r 3 chunks from one to another in a cardinal direction."
				""
				"&bPS: &7Press 'j' for a full screen map, and waypoint management. I wonder if there are other hotkeys too..."
				""
				"&bThis quest unlocks a guide."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:cobaltite_ore"
			id: "0C690272ED4FB1C3"
			rewards: [{
				id: "772D0DF5575FA11B"
				item: "brewinandchewin:jerky"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "rsquare"
			size: 0.66d
			subtitle: "Caves are too scary anyways"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3FA401CACE8BBE5D"
				title: "I will not enter random holes."
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Dont just enter &oany&r random hole..."
			x: 3.3d
			y: -1.32d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["284FF001F6EB9649"]
			description: [
				"&l&8[&6PROJECT-MANAGER&8]&r&r"
				""
				"We are going to need &ba lot&r of wood. Most standard tools have been given an &6upgraded&r version. In fact, your normal iron pickaxe or diamond sword are most likely much &cweaker&r then you would expect. For example, this axe will cut an &a&oENTIRE&r&r tree for you. Top to bottom. The spade, the mining hammer, the &9crowbar,&r the scythe. These tools come with built in features, and gain more durability and damage depending on what material you use. "
				""
				"For your first axe, perhaps &7flint&r might be an easy option?"
			]
